On Sat, May 17, 2014 at 4:37 AM, la durka <durka42@gmail.com> wrote:

> I don't understand the related point. Can you give an example?
>
> Consider:

  (1) mi dunda no da su'o de

  (2) mi dunda be no da su'o de

(1) means that I don't give anything to anyone, while I'm suggesting that
(2) should mean that there's someone to whom I give nothing.

In other words, (1) is:

    no da su'o de zo'u mi da de broda

with broda = "dunda", whereas (2) should be:

  su'o de zo'u mi de brode

with brode = "dunda be no da", where "be no da" is part of the selbri, not
part of the arguments of the main bridi.

mu'o mi'e xorxes

